## Langfuse adds controls for public trace sharing

Source: Langfuse — https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/releases/tag/v4.88.0
Published: 2026-11-26
Channel: github

Langfuse is an AI observability platform that records traces of application activity and groups related activity into sessions. Its release adds controls for organizations and instances to disable public sharing of those records. The change addresses the case where a team wants to stop public links from granting access without rewriting the individual records' saved sharing flags.

An organization owner or administrator can turn off public sharing in the organization settings. Access checks then ignore stored public flags, existing public links no longer grant access, and attempts to publish are rejected. The flags remain stored: turning sharing back on can make previously shared records reachable again, so the interface asks for confirmation. The associated change also describes an instance environment variable that forces the restriction across organizations, subject to a self-hosted enterprise entitlement. Organization-level restrictions also require an eligible entitlement to turn on; a saved restriction continues to apply after a downgrade. The public API still returns the stored public value, and the change does not add a public API for the setting.

Why it matters: Teams sharing traces should review the entitlement and re-enablement behavior before relying on the control.

