## Phoenix adds an API endpoint to retrieve one span

Source: Arize Phoenix — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/arize-phoenix-v22.1.0
Published: 2026-11-26
Channel: github

Phoenix is an open-source platform for tracing and evaluating AI applications. A span is the record of one operation within a trace. Its latest release adds an API endpoint for retrieving one span by identifier, giving clients a direct way to request a specific operation record. A caller supplies the span identifier in the endpoint path and sends a GET request. The release notes identify the new endpoint but do not describe a measured performance improvement or a broader change to trace collection.

Why it matters: Engineers integrating with Phoenix can check the endpoint when they need a specific span by identifier.

